WEBVTT

00:00.350 --> 00:14.378
This is the Services dashboard, signed in as a support tech. Until now you only saw your own days under My Availability. Under Events and Schedule there is a new page, Who's On. Click it.

00:15.178 --> 00:25.705
The top line tells you which schedule is out and when it was published. If today is not covered yet, it says so, and names the day the schedule starts.

00:26.505 --> 00:38.025
The day card shows one day at a time: each shift line with the name on it, from the eight-to-four through the night line. Field Ops Travel carries the location beside the name, and Vacation shows who is out.

00:38.825 --> 00:48.830
Use the arrows to move a day at a time. If a line still needs someone, it shows how many spots are open. Once today is on the schedule, Back to today brings you straight back.

00:49.630 --> 01:00.706
Below the day card is the full two-week grid: one row per shift line, one column per day. It is the same picture you used to get as a screenshot, except this one is live.

01:01.506 --> 01:09.813
Click any day header in the grid and the day card jumps to that day. When you are on the board, your own name is highlighted, so you can find yourself at a glance.

01:10.613 --> 01:19.912
The My availability button takes you back to your own yes-or-no page. Pick the schedule that is out, and a See who's on link takes you straight back to the board.

01:20.712 --> 01:32.833
Nothing on this page can be edited. It is the published schedule, read-only, and it updates the moment the board changes. When a schedule is published, it is live for everyone. No more waiting for the screenshot.
